{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00652",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.77,
      "end_seconds": 13.48,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I do apologise for troubling you, but my voice has gone. It's been a little over a week now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.8,
      "end_seconds": 26.51,
      "duration_seconds": 11.71,
      "text": "Good afternoon. Not at all. Let me hear you. Can you say your name and where you live? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.69,
      "end_seconds": 37.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Margaret Ashworth, number twelve, Birch Road. You can see it's quite croaky. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.53,
      "end_seconds": 47.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "I can hear it, a bit husky. When did it come on, exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.12,
      "end_seconds": 56.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Ten days ago, rather suddenly. I woke up and it simply wasn't there, I could only whisper."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.74,
      "end_seconds": 65.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Had you been ill, a cold or a cough, beforehand? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.43,
      "end_seconds": 78.1,
      "duration_seconds": 10.67,
      "text": "Nothing at all. I'd been to my choir the night before, mind you, and we did the whole of the Messiah. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.24,
      "end_seconds": 90.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Ah. Enthusiastic singing could do that. And how has it been since? Is it improving or staying the same? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.36,
      "end_seconds": 100.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "A little better in the mornings, but by the evening it's worse again. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.58,
      "end_seconds": 110.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Do you have any pain in your throat, or difficulty swallowing? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.35,
      "end_seconds": 120.51,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "No pain to speak of, and I can swallow perfectly well. It's just the voice. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.64,
      "end_seconds": 129.84,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Right. You're not on any regular treatment I should know about? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.08,
      "end_seconds": 140.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "No, I'm very fortunate. I take nothing at all, except a vitamin on Sundays. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.71,
      "end_seconds": 147.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Good. Any other health conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.27,
      "end_seconds": 153.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "I have a touch of acid reflux, nothing major."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.33,
      "end_seconds": 162.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "That's useful. Open wide and say ahh for me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.84,
      "end_seconds": 175.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Ahh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.41,
      "end_seconds": 186.3,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Throat looks fine. The vocal cords are inside, so I can't see them from here. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.41,
      "end_seconds": 193.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Quite so. What do you think it is? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.11,
      "end_seconds": 205.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "A sudden husky voice after heavy use, with some reflux in the background, looks most like laryngitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.34,
      "end_seconds": 211.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Laryngitis. Is that serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.75,
      "end_seconds": 220.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "Not usually. The cords are inflamed, like a sprained ankle, and they need to rest. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.78,
      "end_seconds": 229.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "I see. Then I shall be silent on the subject of Handel. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.06,
      "end_seconds": 239.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "Exactly, no singing, and avoid whispering too, which strains the cords just as much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.24,
      "end_seconds": 244.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Whispering is bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.91,
      "end_seconds": 258.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.59,
      "text": "Yes, a gentle, easy speaking voice is better. Drink plenty of water, and avoid shouting or clearing your throat. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.05,
      "end_seconds": 265.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "I do clear my throat a great deal. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.77,
      "end_seconds": 270.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Try sipping water instead. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.62,
      "end_seconds": 277.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "How long until it improves? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.79,
      "end_seconds": 295.47,
      "duration_seconds": 14.68,
      "text": "Often a couple of weeks. If it's not back to normal in three weeks, I'd like you seen by a specialist who can look at the cords directly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.38,
      "end_seconds": 301.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Three weeks, understood. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.39,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Rest that voice. ~"
    }
  ]
}
